  "id": "DrugBank_DB01005 - MONDO_20541",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxyurea appears to be linked to Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary through a chain of indications involving Melphalan, which is a chemotherapy agent. The evidence suggests that Hydroxyurea may be associated with a broader category of ovarian tumors, including those linked to Hereditary Site-specific Ovarian Cancer Syndrome and Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor Of Ovary. This implies a potential role for Hydroxyurea in the treatment or pathogenesis of these tumors, possibly through shared mechanisms or indirect pathways involving Melphalan. The recurring use of Melphalan as a downstream agent in multiple pathways suggests a possible therapeutic or pathophysiological link between Hydroxyurea and these tumors. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Melphalan in mediating the relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear.",
